{"name":"Grey Clouds","hex":"#b7b7b2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"},{"term":"clouds","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of cloud"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of cloud"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clouds"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nuages gris","blocks":[{"text":"Nuages gris, S.199 or Trübe Wolken, is a work for piano solo composed by Franz Liszt on August 24, 1881. It is one of Liszt's most experimental works, representing, according to Allen Forte, \"a high point in the experimental idiom with respect to expressive compositional procedure.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Franz_Liszt_by_Nadar%2C_March_1886.png/330px-Franz_Liszt_by_Nadar%2C_March_1886.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuages_gris","wikidata":"Q916109"},{"title":"Cloud","blocks":[{"text":"In meteorology, a cloud is an aerosol consisting of a visible mass of miniature liquid droplets, ice crystals, or other particles, suspended in the atmosphere of a planetary body or similar space. Water, primarily, comprises the droplets and crystals. On Earth, clouds are formed as a result of saturation of the air when it is cooled to its dew point, or when it gains sufficient moisture, usually in the form of water vapor, from an adjacent source to raise the dew point to the ambient temperature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/ISS-40_Thunderheads_near_Borneo.jpg/330px-ISS-40_Thunderheads_near_Borneo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloud","wikidata":"Q8074"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/NuagesGrisOpening.PNG/500px-NuagesGrisOpening.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/NuagesGrisOpening.PNG/500px-NuagesGrisOpening.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The first two bars present the quartal harmony used in this piece.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANuagesGrisOpening.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Dreamy_Twilight.jpg/500px-Dreamy_Twilight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Dreamy_Twilight.jpg/1280px-Dreamy_Twilight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Dreamy_Twilight.jpg/500px-Dreamy_Twilight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Windy evening twilight enhanced by the Sun's angle. Clouds can visually mimic a tornado resulting from orographic lift.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADreamy_Twilight.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Cirrus-fibratus.jpg/500px-Cirrus-fibratus.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki